("zaha-hadid-architects","Zaha Hadid Architects","https://www.zaha-hadid.com/","Zaha Hadid Architects was founded in London in 1980 by Zaha Hadid, the first woman to win the Pritzker Prize.","The letters ZHA are cut into angled pieces, echoing the sharp, fluid forms of her buildings.","Initials keep a long name compact on drawings and site boards.",[("cut strokes",0.15,0.2),("initials",0.55,0.05),("angles",0.85,0.85)]),
("big","BIG","https://big.dk/","Bjarke Ingels Group was founded in Copenhagen in 2005 and now also works from New York, London, and Barcelona.","Three abstract shapes on a baseline spell B I G, like a section drawing of three buildings.","Read as letters or as architecture, it rewards a second look.",[("geometric B",0.1,0.15),("baseline",0.5,0.95),("shapes as letters",0.85,0.2)]),
("foster-partners","Foster + Partners","https://www.fosterandpartners.com/","Foster + Partners was founded in London in 1967 by Norman Foster and designed the Gherkin and Apple Park.","A plus sign replaces the ampersand, a small engineering-like detail.","Bold, plain type mirrors the firm's clean high-tech buildings.",[("plus sign",0.53,0.5),("bold sans",0.15,0.15),("founder's name",0.15,0.9)]),
("oma","OMA","https://www.oma.com/","The Office for Metropolitan Architecture was founded in 1975 by Rem Koolhaas and partners and is based in Rotterdam.","Three heavy letters set very tight form a single dense block.","The round O and A make the block feel solid, not aggressive.",[("heavy caps",0.15,0.2),("tight spacing",0.55,0.05),("three letters",0.85,0.85)]),
("herzog-and-de-meuron","Herzog & de Meuron","https://www.herzogdemeuron.com/","Herzog & de Meuron was founded in Basel in 1978 by Jacques Herzog and Pierre de Meuron and designed Tate Modern.","The ampersand and the lowercase d keep the founders' initials honest to their real names.","Heavy type in a short abbreviation is easy to spot on a busy page.",[("ampersand",0.35,0.5),("lowercase d",0.6,0.05),("heavy type",0.9,0.9)]),
("renzo-piano-building-workshop","Renzo Piano Building Workshop","https://www.rpbw.com/","Renzo Piano Building Workshop has offices in Genoa, Paris, and New York and designed the Shard and the Centre Pompidou.","Four serif capitals stand for a long name that calls the studio a workshop, not a firm.","Heavy serifs give the initials a crafted, almost carved feel.",[("serif caps",0.15,0.2),("four initials",0.55,0.05),("heavy serifs",0.85,0.85)]),
("snohetta","Snøhetta","https://www.snohetta.com/","Snøhetta was founded in Oslo in 1989 and is named after a Norwegian mountain.","A small hand-drawn mountain sits after the name, literally drawing what the word means.","The Norwegian ø stays in the wordmark, keeping the local identity.",[("Norwegian ø",0.17,0.15),("light sans",0.45,0.95),("mountain",0.95,0.3)]),
("mvrdv","MVRDV","https://www.mvrdv.com/","MVRDV was founded in Rotterdam in 1993 and is named after its founders Winy Maas, Jacob van Rijs, and Nathalie de Vries.","Condensed heavy capitals turn five initials into a tall, compact block.","The name is a code made from initials, so the type has to be strong.",[("founders' initials",0.5,0.05),("condensed",0.15,0.85),("heavy",0.9,0.9)]),
