("sweco","Sweco","https://www.sweco.se/","Sweco is a Swedish engineering and architecture consultancy based in Stockholm.","A small figure standing inside a house shape puts people at the centre of the brand.","Wide, heavy capitals keep the name sturdy.",[("figure in a house",0.92,0.15),("wide caps",0.3,0.3),("black",0.4,0.95)]),
("nikken-sekkei","Nikken Sekkei","https://www.nikken.co.jp/en/","Nikken Sekkei traces its roots to 1900 in Osaka and designed the Tokyo Skytree.","Thin, widely spaced capitals give the name a light, engineered feel.","A small tagline underneath explains what the firm stands for.",[("thin caps",0.15,0.15),("tagline",0.5,0.95),("wide spacing",0.85,0.25)]),
("kengo-kuma-and-associates","Kengo Kuma & Associates","https://kkaa.co.jp/en/","Kengo Kuma & Associates was founded in Tokyo in 1990 and designed the Japan National Stadium for the Tokyo Olympics.","The letters K K A A are drawn with thin lines, like timber slats in his buildings.","The logo is almost an architectural sketch rather than type.",[("line letters",0.1,0.2),("KKAA",0.5,0.05),("hairlines",0.85,0.85)]),
("henning-larsen","Henning Larsen","https://henninglarsen.com/","Henning Larsen was founded in Copenhagen in 1959 and designed the Harpa concert hall in Reykjavík.","The name is stacked and offset, with a long dash closing the second line.","Bold, plain type gives a Scandinavian firm a confident voice.",[("stacked name",0.1,0.15),("long dash",0.9,0.8),("offset lines",0.45,0.95)]),
("woods-bagot","Woods Bagot","https://www.woodsbagot.com/","Woods Bagot was founded in Adelaide in 1869 and is now a global studio.","Wide, heavy capitals stretch two surnames into one strong line.","Black and plain, the logo works on any project board.",[("wide caps",0.15,0.15),("two names",0.6,0.1),("black",0.85,0.9)]),
("populous","Populous","https://populous.com/","Populous is a Kansas City-based firm known for stadiums such as Wembley and Yankee Stadium.","Wide geometric capitals with round O's echo the shape of a stadium bowl.","The name itself means crowded, a smart fit for venue design.",[("wide caps",0.15,0.15),("round O's",0.18,0.9),("stadium firm",0.8,0.15)]),
